WEBVTT

00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:40.875
Now that you are officially students at DWMA,

00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:42.917
I hope we can all work together

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.375
to hold fast to what we believe to be right,

00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:49.500
and foster pride in being students at DWMA.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.042
Weapons and meisters such as yourselves--

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:21.333
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:32.208
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:43.208
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:01:43.208 --> 00:01:51.208
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:01:51.208 --> 00:01:58.250
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:08.417
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:15.792
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:23.250
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:30.417
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:35.000
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.125
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.542
DWMA's cafeteria serves
students from around the world,

00:02:48.542 --> 00:02:51.000
and there's so many things here,
I can't make up my mind.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.583
Huh?

00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:55.333
Meme, that was fast! And not very balanced.

00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:57.875
Oh? Not as bad as Miss Anya.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.583
Wow...

00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:04.125
She goes wherever her heart
leads her, even for breakfast.

00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:08.458
Maybe we should cook for ourselves for supper.

00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:09.667
For ourselves?

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.500
We're eating breakfast and
lunch in the cafeteria already.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.583
And we can save some of our work proceeds.

00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:15.500
I'm sorry.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.542
Oh! Ma'am? What's the matter?

00:03:18.542 --> 00:03:20.833
Tsugumi, I'm sorry!

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.750
Huh?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.750
As it happens, I saw you getting
your money taken from you

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:29.167
by the witch of the girls' dorm,
but I was too scared to stop her.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:30.542
Oh...

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:32.125
It's my treat today.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:35.125
"The Witch of the Girls' Dorm!"

00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:38.583
So the witch of the girls' dorm
isn't the housemaster,

00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:41.208
she's that cute upperclassman, right?

00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:46.917
Her name is Kim Diehl.
She's in the same class as me.

00:03:46.917 --> 00:03:49.792
When we first started school,
she had long, shiny hair,

00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:53.000
and the cutest appearance,
and was quite the object of attention.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.917
But due to her bad behavior,
people soon steered clear of her.

00:03:57.917 --> 00:04:01.250
What did she do that was so bad, for example?

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.500
All of you, go ahead
and call me by my name.

00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:10.083
--Enyakora--
--Eternal Feather.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.958
What do you think?

00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:14.292
I-It's a pretty name, isn't it?

00:04:14.292 --> 00:04:16.542
It's embarrassing, huh?

00:04:16.542 --> 00:04:18.875
Yes, it is.

00:04:18.875 --> 00:04:21.500
Miss Kim is the one who gave me this name.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.917
Huh?

00:04:22.917 --> 00:04:27.708
DWMA is a unique school,
so one can choose a stage name.

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.917
In fact, we even have a
student who uses "Soul Eater,"

00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:32.958
of all the ridiculous names there are.

00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:36.708
This goes back to the time
when we started school here, but...

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:39.625
You're so plain, you should
take on a stage name.

00:04:39.625 --> 00:04:41.917
Do you really think so?

00:04:41.917 --> 00:04:44.833
This girl's name is Eternal Feather, everyone!

00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:47.083
Huh? H-Hold on!

00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:52.500
And so, she submitted a stage
name form to the school for me,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.292
which can't be changed
again for two whole years.

00:04:56.292 --> 00:04:57.750
And then...

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.875
Name change fee, please.

00:04:59.875 --> 00:05:01.750
What a fiend.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.583
Oh, speak of the devil...

00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:10.125
She's talking to that boy about something.

00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:13.083
Maybe she still maintains
some of her popularity.

00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:16.458
That's Ox Ford. He's in the same class as me.

00:05:16.458 --> 00:05:20.542
He's an elite, with the top grades in our year.

00:05:20.542 --> 00:05:24.000
Most of the boys keep clear of Miss Kim,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.458
but apparently, Ox at least
continues to be on the attack.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.125
Oh, Sid-<i>sensei</i>,

00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:37.125
It looks like that Traitor
bunch has shown up again.

00:05:37.125 --> 00:05:39.083
What? Again?

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:42.792
That's 16 times this month alone.

00:05:42.792 --> 00:05:44.292
That's an awful lot.

00:05:44.292 --> 00:05:46.292
Sid-<i>sensei</i>...

00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:50.000
These Traitor guys just want
to test their own strength, right?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.000
We could just drive them off
with an appropriate show of strength.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.458
We have some free time
before noon, so we could go.

00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:58.958
Oh, yeah? Thanks.

00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:02.583
Akane, Clay...

00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:06.458
Originally being in the
EAT class, you two should be fine,

00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:08.167
but don't get careless.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.792
Right.

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:16.917
Huh?

00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:21.083
There are only two of the strawberry
tarts that the teacher recommended.

00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:24.208
I'll get one next time; you two have these.

00:06:26.208 --> 00:06:28.792
Well, I think I'll refrain, as well.

00:06:28.792 --> 00:06:29.917
Me, too.

00:06:29.917 --> 00:06:33.542
Huh? It's okay for you to take them.

00:06:33.542 --> 00:06:35.625
Oh, the chime.

00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:38.167
All three of us will have
one together next time.

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:39.792
Yes, indeed.

00:06:44.708 --> 00:06:47.250
Tsugumi, class is starting.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.917
Oh, mm-hmm!

00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:51.667
Is that him?

00:06:54.333 --> 00:06:56.167
Did you...

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.875
...sleep well last night?

00:06:58.875 --> 00:06:59.708
Clay...

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:00.875
Yeah.

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:08.167
If you thrust my point at him to
threaten him, he'll soon back down.

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:09.833
Yeah, all right.

00:07:11.917 --> 00:07:14.250
This fight is over.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.083
Give up and go home.

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:20.292
Hey!

00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:27.417
What's with this guy?

00:07:27.417 --> 00:07:31.208
DWMA is divided broadly
into two kinds of courses.

00:07:31.208 --> 00:07:34.625
You all, like 90 percent of the students here,

00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:36.583
are attending the noncombatant classes--

00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:40.708
"Normally Overcome Target," or "NOT" for short.

00:07:40.708 --> 00:07:42.917
Some of you in the future
will advance to use your abilities

00:07:42.917 --> 00:07:45.167
in classes for those who fight against evil,

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:51.500
known as "Especially
Advantaged Talent," or "EAT."

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.333
However, despite being called NOT,
it will be extremely dangerous

00:07:54.333 --> 00:07:57.125
if you are unable to
control your weapon abilities.

00:07:57.125 --> 00:08:00.708
You may end up injuring
people in unexpected ways.

00:08:00.708 --> 00:08:03.625
As such, being weapons,
you will sometimes be feared,

00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:07.333
sometimes avoided, and discriminated against.

00:08:07.333 --> 00:08:09.417
Sorry we're so late.

00:08:09.417 --> 00:08:11.583
He was playing around at the game center.

00:08:11.583 --> 00:08:12.958
Again?!

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:15.292
The game center? That's outrageous!

00:08:15.292 --> 00:08:16.458
Whoa...

00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:17.625
How did it go?

00:08:17.625 --> 00:08:21.042
This man was creepy, and acting weird somehow.

00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:24.125
Normally, we would have just sent him home,

00:08:24.125 --> 00:08:26.167
but just to be safe, he's in custody.

00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:29.125
I see. Good work.

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:31.833
Sit down. I'll continue the class.

00:08:31.833 --> 00:08:35.583
Clay looks so serious,
but he's a little ditzy, huh?

00:08:35.583 --> 00:08:37.375
You think so?

00:08:37.375 --> 00:08:40.208
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:08:40.208 --> 00:08:41.333
See?

00:08:41.333 --> 00:08:43.000
You're right.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.375
Hello!

00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:49.667
Death Deliveries. I'm here
to deliver some coffee beans.

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:50.917
Good work.

00:08:50.917 --> 00:08:52.125
Oh? Ox--

00:08:52.125 --> 00:08:53.292
--sir!

00:08:53.292 --> 00:08:54.458
Ow!

00:08:54.458 --> 00:08:57.500
Ox, sir, are you working, too?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.667
That's surprising.

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:02.500
Yeah, I suppose. I see you
two are hard at work, too.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.292
He's an honor student <i>and </i>a big spender, huh?

00:09:05.292 --> 00:09:08.083
I wonder if he is financing
the witch of the girls' dorm, too.

00:09:08.083 --> 00:09:09.333
Shh!

00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:12.375
Shee? What does that mean?

00:09:12.375 --> 00:09:13.500
Huh?

00:09:16.375 --> 00:09:19.792
Business is slowing down;
you can take your breaks now.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.292
Okay.

00:09:21.292 --> 00:09:23.750
I poured you some tea.
You can drink it in the back.

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:28.875
This is delicious.

00:09:28.875 --> 00:09:30.958
I can't tell.

00:09:30.958 --> 00:09:32.208
It smells so good.

00:09:32.208 --> 00:09:33.958
Quite relaxing, huh?

00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:35.417
Yes.

00:09:40.875 --> 00:09:42.958
Excuse me, Master?

00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:44.250
Hmm?

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.833
You said that the customers
who come to this shop

00:09:46.833 --> 00:09:49.958
are here to see DWMA students.

00:09:49.958 --> 00:09:51.875
Mm-hmm.

00:09:51.875 --> 00:09:55.125
I think they come here to drink
the coffee you make, Master!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.333
You mean, you've never cooked before?

00:10:11.333 --> 00:10:14.167
I was never allowed into the kitchen.

00:10:14.167 --> 00:10:16.417
High-class young lady!

00:10:17.042 --> 00:10:18.833
I am not!

00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:19.917
What about you, Tsugumi?

00:10:19.917 --> 00:10:20.708
Huh?

00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:22.333
What's your specialty dish?

00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:23.917
Shee!

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:39.583
The kitchen belongs to everyone, so...

00:10:39.583 --> 00:10:42.083
I didn't say anything, did I?

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:44.167
Pardon the intrusion.

00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:51.500
Kim, ma'am...

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.958
Hmm?

00:10:53.875 --> 00:10:57.625
Um... would you like to eat with us?

00:10:57.625 --> 00:10:58.458
Huh?

00:10:58.458 --> 00:10:59.875
Eh?

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.042
Why?

00:11:04.042 --> 00:11:07.667
Oh, I just meant,
we're sure to have leftover curry,

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.125
and I thought it would
be better than eating alone.

00:11:10.125 --> 00:11:14.333
I didn't mean to, um... I'm sorry.

00:11:14.333 --> 00:11:17.292
If you want me to eat with you, pay me.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:25.583
Then we're having curry today?

00:11:25.583 --> 00:11:27.625
I goofed, and bought a pumpkin.

00:11:27.625 --> 00:11:29.500
Huh? Then what about the potatoes?

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.000
We're going to have pumpkin curry today, huh?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.417
Geez, Miss Meme...!

00:11:37.167 --> 00:11:40.833
Remember, if you can control
your abilities as a weapon,

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:43.500
then you don't have to just
leave the attacking to the meister,

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:48.125
you can also make use of them in daily life,
and even gain a means of locomotion.

00:11:48.125 --> 00:11:50.042
Jacqueline, please begin.

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:51.417
Right.

00:12:08.792 --> 00:12:11.542
Leave it to our seniors in the EAT class!

00:12:11.542 --> 00:12:16.958
All right, split up into pairs.
Meisters, you support the weapons.

00:12:16.958 --> 00:12:18.208
Um...

00:12:18.208 --> 00:12:21.458
In the last class, Miss Meme
paired with you, Miss Tsugumi,

00:12:21.458 --> 00:12:23.042
so today, it will be me, right?

00:12:23.042 --> 00:12:24.625
Huh? Is that right?

00:12:24.625 --> 00:12:28.417
Yes! Take turns. It's important to take turns.

00:12:28.417 --> 00:12:30.458
Well, all right.

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:32.500
Haven't you gotten sorted out yet?

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.125
Anya, come over here.

00:12:34.125 --> 00:12:37.042
There's an unpaired guy
over here, so pair with him.

00:12:38.208 --> 00:12:42.500
--But today... today, Miss Meme... Meme...
--Gagantous.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.042
Okay, let's begin.

00:12:45.042 --> 00:12:47.083
Shall we get started, Meme?

00:12:47.083 --> 00:12:48.750
Yes, let's.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.417
If you wouldn't mind...

00:12:55.417 --> 00:12:56.417
Yeah.

00:12:56.417 --> 00:12:58.000
Hold on, Meme!

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:02.042
Don't touch me there
before I transform! It tickles!

00:13:02.042 --> 00:13:05.250
Oh, yeah? Tsugumi, you're ticklish, are you?

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:06.708
Stop! Not again!

00:13:06.708 --> 00:13:08.417
Okay, let's begin.

00:13:08.417 --> 00:13:09.500
Yeah.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.208
If you laugh like that, we can't get started.

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:14.083
Come on, Meme!

00:13:14.083 --> 00:13:16.292
Coochie-coochie-coochie!

00:13:21.042 --> 00:13:23.042
Have a safe trip home.

00:13:23.042 --> 00:13:24.250
Miss Anya!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:26.417
Let's go home!

00:13:26.417 --> 00:13:27.875
Huh?

00:13:27.875 --> 00:13:31.958
Um, has Miss Anya already left?

00:13:31.958 --> 00:13:33.125
Yeah.

00:13:33.125 --> 00:13:35.167
That's unusual, huh?

00:13:35.167 --> 00:13:38.125
And Miss Anya gets lonesome so easily, too.

00:13:40.792 --> 00:13:45.708
It's fine, really. One of us
has to be split off, anyway.

00:13:45.708 --> 00:13:49.333
The two of them have started
getting so familiar with each other.

00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:54.125
It may be my own fault for still
using "Miss" with both of them.

00:13:54.125 --> 00:13:55.958
But...

00:13:55.958 --> 00:13:58.625
I can't call them anything else!

00:13:58.625 --> 00:14:01.792
If Miss Tsugumi wasn't
so indecisive in the first place...

00:14:01.792 --> 00:14:05.583
At some point, she has to
choose either Miss Meme or myself.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:16.500
You're... a DWMA student, huh?

00:14:22.667 --> 00:14:26.125
Did you... sleep well last night?

00:14:32.042 --> 00:14:35.083
What do you want?

00:14:35.083 --> 00:14:37.000
I found you.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.083
You're a creepy gentleman.

00:14:44.833 --> 00:14:46.375
What is this?!

00:14:48.333 --> 00:14:51.625
You don't appear to be joking around, huh?

00:14:51.625 --> 00:14:55.125
I did flee from the castle all the way to DWMA,

00:14:55.125 --> 00:14:59.375
so things would get dull without
something like this, wouldn't they?

00:14:59.375 --> 00:15:01.042
This is a good chance to
test out the royal karate

00:15:01.042 --> 00:15:03.333
that was drilled into me at the castle.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.000
No fair!

00:15:20.083 --> 00:15:21.583
Dastardly fiend!

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:32.083
Somebody, help me!

00:15:36.917 --> 00:15:38.417
Miss Meme!

00:15:38.417 --> 00:15:40.083
Miss Anya...

00:15:40.875 --> 00:15:43.625
Is that man anyone that we know?

00:15:43.625 --> 00:15:47.250
No, he is a stranger.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.875
Then, I'll let him have it!

00:15:49.875 --> 00:15:53.250
Wait, Miss Meme! He's no ordinary opponent!

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.125
This isn't a normal fight!

00:15:55.125 --> 00:16:01.667
It's all right. I'm so
scatterbrained, I fear nothing.

00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:03.208
Meme, you're too fast...

00:16:03.208 --> 00:16:04.750
Miss Tsugumi...

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.583
Tsugumi, turn into a weapon!

00:16:13.583 --> 00:16:15.917
Huh?! I can't do it so suddenly!

00:16:17.625 --> 00:16:19.083
Tsugumi!

00:16:31.917 --> 00:16:33.417
Stay back!

00:16:43.833 --> 00:16:46.250
Akane! Clay!

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.625
You all stay back.

00:16:48.625 --> 00:16:53.167
Neither they nor we are DWMA agents.

00:16:53.167 --> 00:16:57.250
I doubt we will prove much
of a challenge to a Traitor.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:00.042
Can I ask you to leave now?

00:17:07.417 --> 00:17:11.333
He sure left without too much trouble, huh?

00:17:11.333 --> 00:17:14.125
Miss Anya, are you all right?

00:17:14.125 --> 00:17:15.750
Yeah.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:16.750
Can you get up?

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.042
Yes.

00:17:18.042 --> 00:17:22.167
We'll see her back to the dorm.

00:17:22.167 --> 00:17:25.792
Then, we'll tell Master that
you're taking off from work.

00:17:25.792 --> 00:17:27.292
Please.

00:17:37.042 --> 00:17:39.208
Thanks for everything this week.

00:17:39.208 --> 00:17:42.833
Good work. Give my regards to the others, too.

00:17:42.833 --> 00:17:44.042
Right.

00:17:44.042 --> 00:17:46.042
Come on by, anytime.

00:17:46.042 --> 00:17:48.083
Thank you very much.

00:17:50.625 --> 00:17:54.375
That week went by in a flash, huh?

00:17:54.375 --> 00:17:56.375
Or wait, was it a month?

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:58.542
It was a week.

00:18:01.792 --> 00:18:04.250
Oh, hey, you two!

00:18:05.333 --> 00:18:07.542
Which of you is Miss Tsugumi Harudori?

00:18:07.542 --> 00:18:09.417
I am.

00:18:09.417 --> 00:18:10.667
Here.

00:18:10.667 --> 00:18:14.875
It's the week's allowance that
Kim Diehl took from you the other day.

00:18:14.875 --> 00:18:18.833
Huh? But Ox, sir, you worked for that.

00:18:18.833 --> 00:18:20.208
It's okay.

00:18:20.208 --> 00:18:23.083
After all, the whole reason
I worked was to give this back.

00:18:23.083 --> 00:18:24.417
Oh, wow.

00:18:24.417 --> 00:18:28.167
In return, I hope you won't hold it against Kim.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:34.458
Everyone is afraid of her, and calls
her the witch of the girl's dorm,

00:18:34.458 --> 00:18:37.917
but it looks to me like
she intentionally avoids others.

00:18:37.917 --> 00:18:40.792
I don't know why, though.

00:18:40.792 --> 00:18:45.542
I know it's asking a lot from me,
but can we call this even now?

00:18:45.542 --> 00:18:46.917
Huh?

00:18:46.917 --> 00:18:48.792
Okay, sorry about all of this.

00:18:48.792 --> 00:18:52.417
Please use the money however
you want; don't let it bother you!

00:18:52.417 --> 00:18:55.417
What a dummy.

00:18:55.417 --> 00:18:57.083
Please?

00:18:57.083 --> 00:19:00.750
Ox has it bad for her, huh?

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.542
Still, I can kind of see why.

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:08.708
Kim may be scary,
but I still sort of care about her.

00:19:08.708 --> 00:19:14.625
And I don't believe that anyone who hums
while making food can be a bad person.

00:19:14.625 --> 00:19:16.333
I wouldn't be too sure.

00:19:27.542 --> 00:19:32.167
I wonder if that fingertip claw
was laced with poison or something.

00:19:32.167 --> 00:19:35.083
We're home!

00:19:35.083 --> 00:19:37.917
Miss Anya, that was awful today--

00:19:37.917 --> 00:19:39.375
Hold on!

00:19:39.375 --> 00:19:42.292
Miss Anya, you've been injured, haven't you?!

00:19:42.292 --> 00:19:45.042
This isn't that big a deal.

00:19:45.042 --> 00:19:47.417
Doesn't she look a little pale?

00:19:47.417 --> 00:19:50.208
We should have the school nurse,
Mendoza-<i>sensei</i>, look at her.

00:19:50.208 --> 00:19:52.083
Right, Medusa-<i>sensei.</i>

00:19:53.167 --> 00:19:54.958
You've got a fever, you know!

00:19:54.958 --> 00:19:57.000
I said I'm fine!

00:19:58.125 --> 00:19:59.458
What should we do?

00:19:59.458 --> 00:20:01.792
Hey, newbie, stand aside.

00:20:01.792 --> 00:20:03.583
Oh, Kim, ma'am...

00:20:04.583 --> 00:20:07.583
Blondie, let me see your wound.

00:20:07.583 --> 00:20:08.750
Why are you suddenly--

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.583
Hurry it up. My time's not free.

00:20:11.583 --> 00:20:12.250
Ow!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.042
N-No need to be rough!

00:20:14.042 --> 00:20:15.458
Dom, ma'am!

00:20:15.458 --> 00:20:19.542
That's "Kim."

00:20:19.542 --> 00:20:21.750
You sure have silky smooth skin, huh?

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:26.000
What are you talking about?!

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.667
It was just a scratch.
When you came in from outside,

00:20:28.667 --> 00:20:30.708
you felt a little hot, right?

00:20:30.708 --> 00:20:35.542
Huh? Suddenly, I feel better.
Was it just my imagination?

00:20:35.542 --> 00:20:38.875
Kim, ma'am, um, how much for the bandage?

00:20:38.875 --> 00:20:40.750
It's okay. This one's on me.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:41.542
Huh?

00:20:41.542 --> 00:20:43.083
What, do you wanna pay?

00:20:43.083 --> 00:20:45.042
No, that's okay.

00:20:55.625 --> 00:20:57.583
Kim!

00:20:57.583 --> 00:20:59.708
You just pulled something, didn't you?

00:20:59.708 --> 00:21:00.500
Huh?

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.083
What did you do? Don't tell me you--

00:21:02.083 --> 00:21:03.875
Jacqueline, isn't it?

00:21:03.875 --> 00:21:06.083
Don't get too full of yourself,
just because you're in EAT.

00:21:06.083 --> 00:21:07.208
Just a moment!

00:21:07.208 --> 00:21:11.542
If you wanna talk to me anymore,
you'll have to pay for an appointment.

00:21:11.542 --> 00:21:13.083
You straight-laced chick.

00:21:13.083 --> 00:21:14.333
Wha--?!

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.500
Are you still in a quandary?

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:26.750
Mm-hmm. I'm not really
sure I should accept this.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:29.958
All you have to do is not blame Miss Kim, right?

00:21:29.958 --> 00:21:32.667
You can blow it all at once, can't you?

00:21:32.667 --> 00:21:34.583
You, too, Meme?

00:21:34.583 --> 00:21:39.042
If you don't, then all of
Ox's work will have been for nothing.

00:21:39.042 --> 00:21:45.083
Mm-hmm, that's true.
Okay, how about we throw a party?

00:21:45.083 --> 00:21:47.583
We have tomorrow off, and everything!

00:21:47.583 --> 00:21:49.875
I think we should do it at Master's shop!

00:21:49.875 --> 00:21:51.792
Is this your treat, Tsugumi?

00:21:51.792 --> 00:21:53.292
Of course it is!

00:21:53.292 --> 00:21:55.625
Are you two partying again by yourselves?!

00:21:55.625 --> 00:21:56.417
Hmm?

00:21:56.417 --> 00:21:57.833
After all, Miss Tsugumi,

00:21:57.833 --> 00:22:00.750
you and Miss Meme will
just be paired up in class again.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.833
I apologize for what happened
in class today. I'm sorry!

00:22:04.833 --> 00:22:06.417
I know!

00:22:09.667 --> 00:22:14.000
I'll write it down on my arm,
to make sure I don't forget.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:14.292
Here! Now, not even I can forget!

00:22:14.292 --> 00:22:17.292
"Next time is Miss Anya"
Here! Now, not even I can forget!

00:22:19.542 --> 00:22:21.167
Right! Me, either!

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:22.958
"Next time is Anya"

00:22:40.792 --> 00:22:43.208
Next time? For what, again?

00:22:43.208 --> 00:22:44.875
You birdbrain!

00:22:47.417 --> 00:22:51.583
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.583 --> 00:22:58.333
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:19.417
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.417 --> 00:23:23.375
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.375 --> 00:23:31.750
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:35.875
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:35.875 --> 00:23:40.042
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.042 --> 00:23:44.167
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.167 --> 00:23:47.917
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:47.917 --> 00:23:52.042
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.042 --> 00:23:56.167
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.167 --> 00:24:00.458
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.458 --> 00:24:04.500
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:09.833
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:19.583
Things can get chaotic here at DWMA.

00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:22.250
Each of us has our own feelings.

00:24:22.250 --> 00:24:24.500
Tsugumi, what is bothering you?

00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:26.667
As I watch on while quietly doing yoga--

00:24:26.667 --> 00:24:27.750
These are our gym shorts?!

00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:28.792
Miss Anya, how curvy!

00:24:28.792 --> 00:24:29.833
"Next time: Waver, Run!"

00:24:29.833 --> 00:24:32.192
"Next time: Waver, Run!"
What is bothering Miss Tsugumi?
